issue.body:
I am trying to load a child module in another child module as described in the following image.

![routing_issue_rc5](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/6051226/18036348/7a885e2e-6d25-11e6-97af-9c6bf3480086.jpg)

When I tried to load the child module "Material Module" which has it's own routes in "Home Module" it is throwing following error:

browser_adapter.js:84 EXCEPTION: Error: Uncaught (in promise): TypeError: Cannot read property 'import' of undefined

I want to reuse the same "Material Module" in another Parent module in future.

Here is my app.routing.ts:

```
{
        path: '',
        redirectTo: '/gologin',
        pathMatch: 'full'
      },
       {
        path: 'gologin',
        loadChildren: 'app/login/login.module'
      },
       {
        path: 'goHome',
        loadChildren: 'app/home/home.module'
    }
```

My Home.route.ts looks as follows:

```
{
        path: '',
        component: 'HomeComponent',
        children:[
       {
        path: '',
        loadChildren: 'app/Material/Material.module'
    }]}
```

How to resolve these kind of modules loading issue in Angular 2 RC5.

Hi,

I'm try to add name at outlet but I got an exception.
My goal is to load two child's components into MainComponent. (I dont need a route for the other modules).

```
const routes: Routes = [
    {
        path: '',
        component: MainComponent,
        children: [
            { path: '', loadChildren: 'modules/componentA/componentA.module' },
            { path: '', loadChildren: 'modules/componentB/componentB.module', outlet: 'compB' }
        ]
    }
];

export const routing = RouterModule.forChild(routes);
```

MainComponent: 

```
@Component({
    selector: 'my-component',
    template: `<router-outlet></router-outlet>
                <router-outlet name='compB'></router-outlet>`,
})
```

But I got this error: 
TypeError: Cannot read property 'routes' of undefined
at getChildConfig (http://localhost:30814/lib/@angular/router/bundles/router.umd.js:1794:39)

When I try to debug inside angular2-router file, it seems that _loadedConfig is missing from the route object.

Any ideas?
